---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/loren-standing.webp';
import event from '../assets/event.jpg';
import ServiceRows from '../components/ServiceRows.astro';
---
<Base title="Meet Loren Michaels Harris" description="Meet the speaker, coach, writer, and Bathrobe Moments host behind the P3 framework: Pain, Perspective, Possibility.">
<section class="wrap about-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE MESSAGE</p><h1>A life lived.<br/>A story<br/><span class="gold-text">still unfolding.</span></h1><p>Loren Michaels Harris is a speaker, coach, keynote writer, and host of Bathrobe Moments. His work begins with a belief that our experiences can become a way to connect with other people.</p><a class="text-link" href="#story">Meet Loren ↓</a></div><figure><Image src={portrait} alt="Loren smiling while seated on outdoor steps" widths={[400,700,1000]} sizes="(max-width:767px) 100vw, 45vw" loading="eager"/><figcaption>Photograph: Scott R. Gane</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="section story-section" id="story"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM EXPERIENCE TO EXPRESSION</p><h2>What we live through<br/>can help us reach<br/><em>someone else.</em></h2></div><div><p>Loren’s own journey includes foster care and finding his voice as a speaker. That experience informs the way he talks about adversity, self-understanding, and the stories people carry into a room.</p><p>Onstage, he brings those themes into conversations with teams, educators, and communities. In coaching and writing, the work becomes personal: finding the message, giving it structure, and learning how to share it.</p><p>Truth, transparency, and service run through his approach. The starting point is a real person and a real experience.</p><a class="text-link" href="/blog/">Read Loren’s own words ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">THE P3 FRAMEWORK</p><h2>A challenge.<br/>A different view.<br/><span class="gold-text">A way forward.</span></h2><div class="topic-columns"><article><p class="eyebrow">01 / PAIN</p><h3>Name the experience.</h3><p>Start with the challenge, loss, or limitation that shapes how you see yourself and how you show up.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">02 / PERSPECTIVE</p><h3>Look again.</h3><p>Explore the lessons, strengths, and questions inside that experience. Give yourself room to see it differently.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">03 / POSSIBILITY</p><h3>Choose what comes next.</h3><p>Consider the message you want to share and the practical next step you can take.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section dark"><div class="wrap split"><figure><Image src={event} alt="Loren with participants in a group photograph at a community gathering" widths={[400,770]} sizes="(max-width:767px) 100vw, 45vw" loading="lazy"/><figcaption class="metadata">A gathering from Loren’s published photo collection.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">CONNECTION IS THE WORK</p><h2>In the room.<br/>In the conversation.</h2><p>Explore the audience experiences, watch Bathrobe Moments, or tell Loren about the room you’re bringing together.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/services/speaking/">Explore speaking ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/bathrobe-moments/">Meet the show ↗</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">WORK WITH LOREN</p><ServiceRows/></section>
</Base>
